messages.content:
Write authorization-inquiry/v1 from this CURRENT natural brief. Do not answer the source question, infer code behavior, add an expectation, future policy or unprovided premises.
Fields: schemaVersion, mode behavior|conformance, questions:[{id,request,principal?,resource?,operation?,entryHint?,premises:[{text,origin:user}]}], optional policy:{text,origin:user|external-policy,location} only for conformance.
Keep every requested scenario in question.request or a separate question. Optional principal/resource/operation are task wording, never invented code facts. Unspecified facts remain unspecified. Conformance copies the independently supplied policy verbatim.
Unrelated synthetic example: {schemaVersion:'authorization-inquiry/v1',mode:'behavior',questions:[{id:'museum',request:'Can a visitor reserve an exhibit?',premises:[]}]}. This is a structural example with no source answer.

Current mode: conformance
Current user policy: {"text":"Only a space administrator may remove another member from that space. This policy does not prohibit a member leaving the space themselves.","origin":"user","location":"experimental-user-brief:memos-member-policy/v1"}
Current natural brief:
Check DeleteSpaceMember in this Memos revision against the independently supplied current policy. May an ordinary space member remove a different member, and do visible admin and self-removal paths differ? Do not assume deployment middleware or undocumented role grants. Explain actual behavior, compare it with the policy, cite the controlling source and preserve any decisive missing facts.

You MUST respond with a valid JSON object conforming to this schema:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "schemaVersion": {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "authorization-inquiry/v1"
    },
    "mode": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "behavior",
        "conformance"
      ]
    },
    "questions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "request": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "principal": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "resource": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "operation": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "entryHint": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "premises": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "origin": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "const": "user"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "text",
                "origin"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "request",
          "premises"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "policy": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "text": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "origin": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "user",
            "external-policy"
          ]
        },
        "location": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "text",
        "origin",
        "location"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "schemaVersion",
    "mode",
    "questions"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

Output ONLY the JSON object, nothing else. No markdown fences, no explanation.
